+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Lookup backend | Local embedded SQLite index, built and validated on each kiosk from the incoming snapshot | Keeps lookup and snapshot validation entirely on kiosk-local files, consistent with the HLD tenet that lookup requires no runtime network access and kiosks have no network route during normal operation. An on-site HTTPS directory or a managed search service would both require network connectivity the kiosks don't have, plus service-timeout handling, credentials, or recurring cost, for a result type and certificate interface that stay identical either way. The tradeoff accepted is that each kiosk validates and rebuilds its own index on every snapshot import rather than sharing one centrally maintained index. |
